managed to get to bed we  get some sleep we get on the road the  next day I think around noon maybe so  now we're driving out to Wisconsin so  now it's you know we're on the second  half of the trip you know it's all it's  not really all downhill from here  but it's at least you know getting  closer to our destination we're not  gonna have to stay somewhere else that's  not you know where we want to be we will  stay in a hotel the next night but  that's just because the apartment isn't  quite ready yet  so you know that day went pretty pretty  smoothly  there were a few things where it got a  bit dicey in Chicago you know I'm  driving through you know the downtown  I'm 94 and I had some lady it managed to  basically cut me off twice in her  Volkswagen Beetle just not paying  attention at all and not thinking about  the fact that well you know a car or a  pickup truck can stop fairly quickly  it's not smart to you know drive out in  front of a moving truck because these  things take a little bit more time to  come to a spot so there's a bit of load  shifting that takes place during that  time but we managed to get to the hotel  and it turns out that it's the the La  Quinta in Waukesha the very edge of  Waukesha or Waukesha meets Brookfield  technically I think it's Brookfield but  I thought we think of it as Waukesha  because I used to live there and I used  to work at the Kentucky Fried Chicken  which is still there right next to the  La Quinta I would have to ride the bus  from the downtown terminal of Waukesha  out to Kirk  corners and then crossed the interstate  and then actually this is a whole  different story but I would walk back  home along the interstate for a while  and then on highway 18 about three miles  to get back to to my mother's house  after work just silly stuff that went on  during during the late 80s in any case  we you know we get a good night's sleep  and now it's time to meet up with the  other movers the other professionals  that we've got here to go into the  apartment to handle everything to sign  the lease to you know find out about the  amenities and so we go and do all that  and my wife's parents were kind enough  to come out and take care of the dogs  so you know so we don't have them  underfoot and we come out here and it's  you know a beautiful place it's a great  you know I mean being on the road is not  a lot of fun and you know hotels can be  quite nice sometimes but it's not quite  the same thing as being home and you  know here we arrive and we go to the you  know meet the people that we were going  to take care of the paperwork with we  find out about all the different  amenities involved here we can see the  wonderful view out of the the window on  the sixth floor where we're handling  everything and now we're getting quite  excited I think well I think my wife was  already quite excited but now I'm a bit  more excited because you know the things  are really happening but we still have  the the rest of the movement so we've  got the truck you know we go back at the  truck park in the loading zone the  movers arrive therefore actually from  Chicago so I talked back and forth with  them a little bit about where they are  in Chicago and you know my family a lot  of them still live in that area and then  you know it's it's a good five hours of  them more or less just you know  unpacking the trunk onto the street and  then going and using the elevators you  know  take a load after load after load up  here to the apartment and to drop stuff  wha  took quite a bit of time I'm outside for  most of it you know watching man's  apartment you sure nobody comes along  just grabs our stuff and by now you know  I'm not supposed to be you know doing  any idiot lifting because we got these  young guys to do it which is very smart  but I don't think I would have wanted to  lift anything because I'm dog-tired and  you know my back is kind of tied up in  knots from all the driving and and some  of the lifting that I did at other times  the movers were not quite happening the  professional movers the job that the non  professional movers had done in the  middle of the night because they looked  in and they could see things were just  like a lot of kilter they're like what  what is this you know there was a little  bit of swearing involved but overall it  wasn't too bad there was a little bit of  breakage you know a few things that we  lost that's usually going to happen and  any move most of them were fairly minor  things fortunately nothing that can't be  replaced and now we're here so now it's  a matter of bit by bit by bit as as we  you know continue working because and  Andy and I are both you know working a  lot of the time developing new new you  know routines and habits and slowly  unpacking all of these these boxes and  taking things into storage taking things  out of storage we're now at the point  where the kitchen is completely setup  which is great we've got some things you  know we've been looking at what's the  order for as far as you know the things  for the bedroom or the living room we're  not quite sure whether I'm going to  build a bunch of bookshelves or whether  we're going to find some other recourse  we've already started going through the  boxes of books and doing a bit of triage  deciding to take some of them to used  book stores and sell them off the things  that we don't really need or the things  that  and easily get at the library we got  ourselves into a position where we  really do have too many books you know  when you have a marriage of two  academics both of whom you already have  an extensive library and both of whom  are bibliophiles and both of whom are  willing to indulge the other and say hey  let's get some more books you end up  with a lot of books so there's there's  all of that now I said I was going to  mention a little bit why we actually  moved here and then that's fairly  straightforward you know Andy and I are  both from this area I grew up in a  little town called Wales which is quite  a bit west of Milwaukee and is still  fairly countryside although most of the  development of the surrounding area has  been quite developed but at the time  that I grew up it was really a  countryside she grew up closer to  Milwaukee in Brookfield at a time when  there was still a lot of green space in  Brookfield but where you know it's still  a more urban environment Waukesha would  be sort of the dividing line between us  we went to high school together and you  know coming back to this area for us is  really great Andy has lived outside of  Wisconsin in New York for close to two  decades I have been gone from Wisconsin  in a variety of places ranging from  southern Illinois which is really a  whole different state from the rest of  Illinois Indiana North Carolina and then  moving up to New York I have been  outside of Wisconsin for 20 years and so  we're really happy to be back here and  moving in Milwaukee is happening the  city there's there's a lot of great  stuff going on here culturally the food  scene is just amazing there's there's  all sorts of you know great museums and  libraries if we get again to go to  someplace that's a bit bigger Chicago is  just an hour and a half down  and really looking forward to  reconnecting with a lot of old friends  and even some of the family that I don't  get to see that often and he's really  happy because her family is here as well  so she gets to see them you know the  past it was basically holidays and now  we get to see people whatever we want to  and we have the challenge of building up  sort of a new business network and a  network of places to do speaking gigs  and do consulting but we're we're on our  old home turf I mean we did okay out in  New York I was never really in New York  I guess Andy you could say it's arguably  a New Yorker she certainly knew her way  around there but it's something  different when you're back in your you  know original home environment so we're  really looking forward to all the things  we've got coming up here I've already  got one event scheduled for stoical week  in November I'll tell you more about  that in the update video for November  and during stoical week but yeah great  experience a little bit of hiccups  during the move itself but I do have to  say the Penske people as far as their  customer service goes pretty good and  things could have gone a lot worse so  we're really happy to be here I'm happy  you know Andy's happy the dogs are happy  and I'm guessing that you know as we  start meeting up with more and more old  friends and family they're gonna be  pretty happy about it too so that is the  whole story of the move up to this point
 

